        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for snpguest",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for snpguest fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-25541: bytes: integer overflow in 'BytesMut:reserve' can lead to undefined behavior and crashes\n  (bsc#1274139).\n- CVE-2026-41678: openssl: incorrect bounds assertion in AES keywrap can lead to an out-of-bounds write (bsc#1270642).\n- CVE-2026-42327: openssl: missing validation when processing certificates with non-UTF-8 OCSP URLs can lead to\n  undefined behavior (bsc#1270527).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
